          "question": "worst hedache ive ever had, came on like a bang while i was lifting, and the lights hurt",
          "answer": "**Seek emergency care now. Call your local emergency number or go to the nearest emergency department. Do not drive yourself.**\n\nA headache that comes on suddenly, reaches full strength within about a minute, and is described as the worst of your life is listed as an emergency in the \"Sudden severe headache\" guidance (educational summary, emergency medicine and neurology societies). The same guidance lists sudden severe headache with no known cause as a stroke warning sign. Your description matches both.\n\nThe urgency tool returned \"routine\" because none of its fixed rules matched the wording. That result conflicts with the guidance I retrieved, which names this pattern as an emergency. Because missing an emergency is the bigger risk, I am following the guidance.\n\nOther features to tell the emergency team about, without waiting to check them first:\n- Stiff neck, fever, or a rash that does not fade when pressed. The meningitis guidance lists these with severe headache.\n- Confusion, drowsiness, weakness or numbness, trouble speaking, or vision changes. The stroke guidance lists these.\n- Vomiting, or the headache getting worse over the next hours.\n\nYour sensitivity to light is listed in the meningitis guidance, but only alongside fever and headache, and you have not mentioned fever. Do not wait to find out whether these apply.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
